& [Intention]
  + make host portability and attributed multi-host development a product property without confusing one successful deployment with proof for every backend
  + use separate host capability receipts, provider profiles, isolated workspaces, artifact identities, and acceptance evidence rather than shared mutable worktrees

& [Result]
  + [recommended_topology] EVO-X2 is the first candidate for always-on SOP attention audit and coordination while RTX 5090 hosts are candidates for CUDA-backed inner-model inference builds and independent acceptance
  + [portability_boundary] signed SOP contracts Rust logic schemas evidence and deployment manifests should remain common while provider binary driver accelerator process and resource observations remain host-specific
  + [host_3_state] unavailable until assembled inventoried connected and separately admitted
  + [replication_value] the second RTX 5090 host can serve as a clean-room reproducibility recovery and canary target rather than merely duplicating the first mutable environment
  + [concurrency_boundary] no two workers may mutate one worktree; coordination must use isolated clones or worktrees immutable commit identities bounded leases receipts and explicit integration ownership

& [Constraints]
  + user-reported hardware descriptions are planning inputs and require read-only inventory before installation or performance claims
  + NVIDIA CUDA, EVO-X2 accelerator, CPU fallback, driver, llama.cpp, model, memory, disk, trust-root, and service identities remain distinct admission coordinates
  + success on one host does not prove binary portability, performance equivalence, provider availability, or production readiness on another
  + no remote contact, installation, model movement, process launch, host mutation, or authority grant occurs in this discussion turn

& [UnresolvedFrontier]
  + preserve and sign a three-host capability and deployment portability specification when implementation resumes
  + revalidate EVO-X2, inventory the currently assembled RTX 5090 host, and defer the third-host receipt until assembly and connection
  + decide the exact outer coordinator, inner-model worker, independent reviewer, integration owner, failover, and artifact-distribution roles before multi-host autonomy
